<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Desna</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Desna is a river of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a>, about 1,130 km long, which joins the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dnieper">Dnieper</a> just above <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyiv">Kyiv</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bryansk">Bryansk</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/novhorod-siverskyi">Novhorod-Siverskyi</a> and Chernihiv stand on its banks. Its basin was the land of the Severians and later the core of the Principality of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chernigov">Chernigov</a>.</p></div>
